{
  "case_id": "2016-15-1391",
  "document_hash": "050c8e7670756747ba5b1fe307802d717ccb04e6270ec81455d301634d1e2cc8",
  "records": [
    {
      "attribution": "Court",
      "case_id": "2016-15-1391",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "050c8e7670756747ba5b1fe307802d717ccb04e6270ec81455d301634d1e2cc8",
      "evidence_id": "ev-050c8e767075-0000-0000",
      "kind": "procedural_event",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 1,
        "start": 1
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "The above-entitled matter came on for oral argument before the Supreme Court of the United States at 10:04 a.m."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Expressions Hair Design",
      "case_id": "2016-15-1391",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "050c8e7670756747ba5b1fe307802d717ccb04e6270ec81455d301634d1e2cc8",
      "evidence_id": "ev-050c8e767075-0000-0001",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 4,
        "start": 4
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "One of the Petitioners, Expressions Hair Design, is engaging in dual pricing, they're charging two different prices, one for cash, one for credit, but they are trying as hard as they can to describe that as a -- as a discount so that they comply with the law."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Kagan",
      "case_id": "2016-15-1391",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "050c8e7670756747ba5b1fe307802d717ccb04e6270ec81455d301634d1e2cc8",
      "evidence_id": "ev-050c8e767075-0000-0002",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 4,
        "start": 4
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE KAGAN: Mr. Gupta, what -- what speech precisely do you think is being restricted?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Petitioners",
      "case_id": "2016-15-1391",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "050c8e7670756747ba5b1fe307802d717ccb04e6270ec81455d301634d1e2cc8",
      "evidence_id": "ev-050c8e767075-0000-0003",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 5,
        "start": 5
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "chart. And what we'd like to do, ideally, is describe the pastrami sandwich as $10, and then tell you that it's going to cost a certain percentage more, 2 percent more, to pay with a credit card."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Breyer",
      "case_id": "2016-15-1391",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "050c8e7670756747ba5b1fe307802d717ccb04e6270ec81455d301634d1e2cc8",
      "evidence_id": "ev-050c8e767075-0001-0000",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 21,
        "start": 21
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE BREYER: Well, now, this is exactly what's worrying me. The State, you say, told some merchants that they cannot say that they have a surcharge. Is that what it is? Is that the problem?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Court",
      "case_id": "2016-15-1391",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "050c8e7670756747ba5b1fe307802d717ccb04e6270ec81455d301634d1e2cc8",
      "evidence_id": "ev-050c8e767075-0001-0005",
      "kind": "procedural_event",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 28,
        "start": 28
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "ORAL ARGUMENT OF ERIC J. FEIGIN FOR UNITED STATES, AS AMICUS CURIAE, SUPPORTING NEITHER PARTY"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice ALITO",
      "case_id": "2016-15-1391",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "050c8e7670756747ba5b1fe307802d717ccb04e6270ec81455d301634d1e2cc8",
      "evidence_id": "ev-050c8e767075-0002-0000",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 40,
        "start": 40
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Could I just ask you a preliminary question about the division of litigation authority in New York State? Does the attorney general or the solicitor general have the authority under New York law to bind all of the district attorneys in the State to an interpretation of this statute? And has the attorney general issued a -- an official interpretation so that all of the district attorneys will be required to -- to enforce this in the same way?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Petitioners",
      "case_id": "2016-15-1391",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "050c8e7670756747ba5b1fe307802d717ccb04e6270ec81455d301634d1e2cc8",
      "evidence_id": "ev-050c8e767075-0002-0001",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 40,
        "start": 40
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "So the attorney general and the district attorneys are separate authorities under New York law. In this case, however, the relevant district attorneys for the counties where these Petitioners are located are parties to this case --"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice KAGAN",
      "case_id": "2016-15-1391",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "050c8e7670756747ba5b1fe307802d717ccb04e6270ec81455d301634d1e2cc8",
      "evidence_id": "ev-050c8e767075-0002-0002",
      "kind": "allegation",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 41,
        "start": 41
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "But, you know, there does seem to have been a debate about what this statute means. Because I look at some of this enforcement history and I think -- I don't really understand why this violates that law."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Petitioners",
      "case_id": "2016-15-1391",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "050c8e7670756747ba5b1fe307802d717ccb04e6270ec81455d301634d1e2cc8",
      "evidence_id": "ev-050c8e767075-0002-0003",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 42,
        "start": 42
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "attorney general's office, that it confirms sort of the plain reading of this statute in a single-price scheme."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice KENNEDY",
      "case_id": "2016-15-1391",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "050c8e7670756747ba5b1fe307802d717ccb04e6270ec81455d301634d1e2cc8",
      "evidence_id": "ev-050c8e767075-0002-0004",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 42,
        "start": 42
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "But under your view, if the heating oil people had said, it's $103 if you pay by credit card; if you do not pay by credit card, pay by cash, it's $100, that is lawful?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice SOTOMAYOR",
      "case_id": "2016-15-1391",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "050c8e7670756747ba5b1fe307802d717ccb04e6270ec81455d301634d1e2cc8",
      "evidence_id": "ev-050c8e767075-0002-0005",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 44,
        "start": 44
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Is your answer to the reply brief examples the same as the solicitor general's office? And do you have a concern the way it does that the statute could be read more broadly?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice BREYER",
      "case_id": "2016-15-1391",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "050c8e7670756747ba5b1fe307802d717ccb04e6270ec81455d301634d1e2cc8",
      "evidence_id": "ev-050c8e767075-0002-0007",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 46,
        "start": 46
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Go ahead. Are you finished?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice BREYER",
      "case_id": "2016-15-1391",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "050c8e7670756747ba5b1fe307802d717ccb04e6270ec81455d301634d1e2cc8",
      "evidence_id": "ev-050c8e767075-0002-0008",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 47,
        "start": 47
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "That is, you tell me, given precedent, et cetera, what should we overrule? Or what should we narrow?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice ALITO",
      "case_id": "2016-15-1391",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "050c8e7670756747ba5b1fe307802d717ccb04e6270ec81455d301634d1e2cc8",
      "evidence_id": "ev-050c8e767075-0002-0010",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 56,
        "start": 56
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Does this apply to all merchants? Anybody who sells anything?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice BREYER",
      "case_id": "2016-15-1391",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "050c8e7670756747ba5b1fe307802d717ccb04e6270ec81455d301634d1e2cc8",
      "evidence_id": "ev-050c8e767075-0002-0011",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 57,
        "start": 57
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "how then do I distinguish the cases which you've talked about how you -- what you say in respect to price because after all, even if it's just evidentiary, this statute does affect what people say as to price. So if in fact I need a legal distinction here to get at what I think the First Amendment is driving at, what's your best effort?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Ginsburg",
      "case_id": "2016-15-1391",
      "confidence": 0.95,
      "document_hash": "050c8e7670756747ba5b1fe307802d717ccb04e6270ec81455d301634d1e2cc8",
      "evidence_id": "ev-050c8e767075-0003-0000",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 59,
        "start": 59
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "If we -- if we agree with the government that this is because it affects how the merchant characterizes his price, would you also take the position that the government takes that it's justified as a disclosure law?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Kagan",
      "case_id": "2016-15-1391",
      "confidence": 0.95,
      "document_hash": "050c8e7670756747ba5b1fe307802d717ccb04e6270ec81455d301634d1e2cc8",
      "evidence_id": "ev-050c8e767075-0003-0001",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 60,
        "start": 60
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Mr. Wu, you think, is this not true, that the dual pricing scheme is legal; is that right?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Mr. Wu",
      "case_id": "2016-15-1391",
      "confidence": 0.95,
      "document_hash": "050c8e7670756747ba5b1fe307802d717ccb04e6270ec81455d301634d1e2cc8",
      "evidence_id": "ev-050c8e767075-0003-0002",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 60,
        "start": 60
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "That's correct."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Sotomayor",
      "case_id": "2016-15-1391",
      "confidence": 0.95,
      "document_hash": "050c8e7670756747ba5b1fe307802d717ccb04e6270ec81455d301634d1e2cc8",
      "evidence_id": "ev-050c8e767075-0003-0003",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 62,
        "start": 62
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "There is nothing about the scheme that addresses that. The scheme has no disclosure requirement of what was your actual credit card charge versus what you're charging."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Mr. Gupta",
      "case_id": "2016-15-1391",
      "confidence": 0.95,
      "document_hash": "050c8e7670756747ba5b1fe307802d717ccb04e6270ec81455d301634d1e2cc8",
      "evidence_id": "ev-050c8e767075-0003-0004",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 63,
        "start": 63
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "The solicitor general agrees with us that this is a restriction of speech, but posits that the only thing that's left on the table is a disclosure rationale that New York abandoned in the courts below and is barely pressing here, and the problem with that is that this is a criminal speech restriction."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Court",
      "case_id": "2016-15-1391",
      "confidence": 0.95,
      "document_hash": "050c8e7670756747ba5b1fe307802d717ccb04e6270ec81455d301634d1e2cc8",
      "evidence_id": "ev-050c8e767075-0003-0005",
      "kind": "procedural_event",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 64,
        "start": 64
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "The case is submitted. (Whereupon, at 11:07 a.m., the case in the above-entitled matter was submitted.)"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Source extraction",
      "case_id": "2016-15-1391",
      "confidence": 0.0,
